{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Init.Omega"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit52_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit52_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L163-L168","doc":"**The instance of the obstruction**: no symmetric scalar separates the `5₂`\nchiralities, and the datum it must represent is chiral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit41_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit41_eq","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L160-L161","doc":"The `4₁` split satisfies the amphichiral collapse hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit41_amphichiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit41_amphichiral","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L156-L158","doc":"`4₁` is amphichiral: its bar-odd part vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit52_chiral_grading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit52_chiral_grading","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L151-L154","doc":"`5₂` is chiral, with bar-grading `(even, odd) = (7, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit41","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L148-L149","doc":"The `4₁` split: amphichirality forces the two constants to coincide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit52","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.dtSplit52","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L145-L146","doc":"The `5₂` chirality split (literature instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.amphichiral_cannot_witness_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.amphichiral_cannot_witness_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L128-L136","doc":"**A single amphichiral knot cannot exhibit the obstruction.** If the split is\namphichiral, it equals its own mirror, so *every* reading — symmetric or not —\nagrees on it and on its mirror. The cross-knot (chiral) test is therefore a\nlogical necessity, not a methodological preference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.symmetric_scalar_loses_chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.symmetric_scalar_loses_chirality","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L119-L126","doc":"**Consequence.** For a chiral split, a symmetric scalar takes one value while\nthe datum it is meant to represent has a nonzero bar-odd part — so the scalar\ncannot determine the ordered pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.symmetric_scalar_cannot_separate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.symmetric_scalar_cannot_separate","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L106-L117","doc":"**The obstruction, in full generality.** Any symmetric integer reading `g`\nassigns the same value to a split and to its mirror. Hence for a genuinely chiral\nsplit, `g` cannot depend on the chirality at all: every symmetric scalar is blind\nto the `−1` eigenspace, which for a chiral count is nonzero.\n\nThis is the input-free form of\n`FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit.symmetric_scalar_blind_to_chirality`; the knot numbers\nenter only in the instance below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.amphichiral_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.amphichiral_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L97-L104","doc":"**Amphichiral collapse.** If the two constants agree, the bar-odd part is\nzero and the pair is its own mirror — the degenerate case in which a single\nscalar *does* carry the whole datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.not_chiral_iff_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.not_chiral_iff_eq","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L93-L95","doc":"Not-chiral is exactly equality of the two constants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.chiral_iff_odd_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.chiral_iff_odd_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L89-L91","doc":"**Chirality is exactly nonvanishing of the bar-odd part.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.instDecidableIsChiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.instDecidableIsChiral","kind":"instance","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L86-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.IsChiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.IsChiral","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L83-L84","doc":"A split is **genuinely chiral** when its two constants differ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barGrading_faithful_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barGrading_faithful_general","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L77-L81","doc":"**The `ℤ/2` grading is faithful** — no information is lost in passing to the\nbar-even/bar-odd parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barOdd_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barOdd_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L73-L75","doc":"`τ` negates the bar-odd part: it is the `−1` eigenvector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barEven_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barEven_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L69-L71","doc":"`τ` fixes the bar-even part: it is the `+1` eigenvector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barOdd","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L66-L67","doc":"The `τ`-negated (bar-odd) part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.barEven","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The `τ`-fixed (bar-even) part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.mirror_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.mirror_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L59-L61","doc":"`τ` is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.mirror","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L56-L57","doc":"The mirror involution `τ` exchanging the two chiralities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.Split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ChiralityGradedCount.Split","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ChiralityGradedCount.lean#L53-L54","doc":"A chirality-split count: the ordered pair of `S⁺` and `S⁻` constants. ","signatureChunk":0}]}